# What the device actually does

Measured rather than asserted. Generated from the readings in
[resources/sweeps/](../resources/sweeps/), so no figure here can drift from the
file it came from.

This is the data the guessing was standing in for. A character word used to move
a control by an amount somebody typed;
[docs/algorithm.md](algorithm.md) says what replaces that.

## Two files, answering two questions

`fingerprints.json` says **what each block sounds like**. One reading per block,
sitting at its own defaults, for {{ .Blocks }} of them. That is what picking a
block needs: ranking {{ .Amps }} amplifiers by how close each sits to a target
turns "sound like this record" into a shortlist.

`<model>.json` says **what one block's controls do**. Every control swept across
the range the catalog gives it, folded into slopes. That is what setting a chain
needs once the chain is picked.

The split is a cost one. A control is about two minutes, so a fingerprint for
everything and curves for the blocks a chain reaches for is the only affordable
shape.

Every reading here was taken against one signal, `{{ .Reference.File }}`,
identified by its hash inside each file. A different one invalidates every
number taken against the old one.

